(load "parsec.carp")
(load "parsec_docs.carp")

(Project.config "title" "parsec")
(Project.config "docs-directory" "./docs/")
(Project.config "docs-logo" "")
(Project.config "docs-url" "https://github.com/carpentry-org/parsec")
(Project.config "docs-styling" "../style.css")
(Project.config "docs-prelude" "A Parsec-style parser combinator library
for Carp.

`Parser` is a closure-in-struct holding a `run` function over an input
string and a position cursor. Build parsers from primitives
([`byte`](./Parser.html#byte), [`satisfy`](./Parser.html#satisfy),
[`string`](./Parser.html#string), ...), combine them with
[`map`](./Parser.html#map), [`seq`](./Parser.html#seq),
[`alt`](./Parser.html#alt), [`many`](./Parser.html#many), and friends,
and run with [`parse`](./Parser.html#parse).

Backtracking follows Parsec semantics: alternation only retries when
the left branch fails *without consuming*. Wrap with
[`try`](./Parser.html#try) for full backtracking.

### Quick start
```
(load \"git@github.com:carpentry-org/parsec@0.3.0\")

(let [p (Parser.between (Parser.byte \\[)
                        (Parser.byte \\])
                        (Parser.Lexer.integer))]
  (match (Parser.parse p \"[42]\")
    (Result.Success n) (println* &n)
    (Result.Error e)   (IO.errorln &(Parser.format-error &e))))
```

### Modules
- [`Parser`](./Parser.html) — primitives, combinators, entry point
- [`Parser.UTF8`](./Parser.UTF8.html) — codepoint-level parsers
- [`Parser.Lexer`](./Parser.Lexer.html) — common tokens (integer, identifier, ...)
- [`Cursor`](./Cursor.html), [`ParseErr`](./ParseErr.html), [`Expected`](./Expected.html), [`Reply`](./Reply.html) — supporting types

### Guides
- [Tutorial](./Tutorial.html) — build an arithmetic expression parser step by step.
- [Pitfalls](./Pitfalls.html) — concrete gotchas, ordered by how often they bite.")

(save-docs Parser Cursor ParseErr Expected Reply Tutorial Pitfalls)
;; Carp's save-docs hardcodes the index filename as <title>_index.html.
;; Rename to docs/index.html.
(defn main [] (System.system "mv ./docs/parsec_index.html ./docs/index.html"))
